<description>
Complete the partially shown horizontal motif by repeating its minimal column period across the grid.

Input structure
The input is a rectangular grid with a dominant background color and a
foreground motif drawn from the left edge across part of the rows.

Rule
Find the smallest column period for which all visible foreground pixels agree
by row and column residue, then repeat that period across the full width.

Key insight
The background cells to the right are not empty final cells; they are the
missing later copies of the same minimal horizontal tile already visible at
the left.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "left-edge prefix of a horizontal periodic foreground motif on the background",
  "dst": "missing right-side suffix columns of the same full-width grid",
  "transform": "infer the minimal column period consistent with all visible foreground pixels by row and column residue, then repeat that tile across the full width"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5 rows x 15 cols, background 0 [observed]
  tile:
    period: 3-6 columns
    structure: bottom-heavy staircase; bottom row fully filled, each row's fg columns are superset of row above
    active_rows: 2-3 (always at the bottom of the grid), top rows all background
    fg_colors: 2-3 distinct non-zero colors
    each_column: monochromatic (all fg pixels in a column share one color)
    row_fg_counts: non-decreasing from top to bottom (e.g. 0,0,0,2,3 or 0,0,1,3,4)
    fg_contiguous_per_row: not required (train_2 has split fg in rows, e.g. cols {0,5})
  input_prefix:
    shows: 1-2 full repeats + 0-4 partial columns of the tile, starting from col 0
    visible_cols: period+1 to 2*period+2 (always > period so at least one full repeat plus some extra)
    remaining_cols: all background (clean vertical cutoff)
  output: tile repeated across full 15-col width (last repeat may be truncated)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick period P in [3,6] and grid 5x15 with bg=0
    2. Pick K active rows (2-3) anchored at the bottom of the grid
    3. Build a P-wide tile column by column; bottom row gets all P cols filled;
       each row above gets a (strict or equal) subset of columns from the row below;
       row fg counts must be non-decreasing top-to-bottom
    4. Assign 2-3 distinct non-zero colors to tile cells; each column uses one color
    5. Tile the full 15-col output by repeating the P-wide tile
    6. Choose a cutoff C in [P+1, min(2*P+2, 14)] so input shows >=1 full repeat plus partial
    7. Input = output with columns C..14 replaced by background
```
